{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (RNA-only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) achieved only ~48.5% accuracy, establishing a weak baseline. The most critical uncertainty at this stage is which modality (RNA vs. image) carries the most discriminative signal for this task, as this determines the entire branch of the config space to prioritize over the remaining 8 experiments. Question: config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) directly parallels config_001 with the modality swapped, isolating the effect of modality while holding profile setting and aggregation constant. Why: Resolving the modality question early is the highest-leverage decision—if image substantially outperforms RNA, I can focus remaining budget on image encoders and multimodal fusion; if RNA is stronger, I can invest in better RNA encoders (scgpt, scvi) and aggregation; if they are comparable, multimodal fusion becomes the key direction. This single experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the dominant design axis with a clean, single-variable comparison."
}

